A||N||5||85blackgt||dropping the cradle||||11||
Z||000000||85blackgt||05-30-2001||11:06 AM||||ive been trying to remove the cradle bolts to drop the engine in my gt now,iv eremoved both bolts on the rear now the ones im having trouble with are the ones in the back with the rubber mounts. ive got the nuts off but the bolt just keeps turning and it dosen't look like its going any where ive tried to hammmer it out and it wont move!<BR>i need help quickly!! if not ill cut them off thanks! ||||reg||11
Z||000001||Oreif||05-30-2001||11:53 AM||||Soak them in WD-40 or liquid wrench or rust buster type of spray. They are probably corroded to the sleeve inside the bushing.<BR>Spray them down and let them sit then install the nut to protect the threads and pound back and forth with a hammer. Eventually the bolt will start to wiggle and come free. It takes a while but it can be done. The easiest way is to cut them and get new bolts.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Scott||05-30-2001||12:15 PM||||Don't waste too much time trying to free them.  Afew years ago I spent 6 hours trying to free one front craddle bolt. (I got kinda anal retentive 'bout it!)  It was a total waste of time.  If it doesn't come loose in a few minutes cut it.  And don't forget to put antisieze on the bolts when you reinstall them. ||||reg||10
Z||000003||85blackgt||05-30-2001||12:50 PM||||thanks guys i was out in the garage for about an hour and they wont come loose so i cut them one more question,i kinda chopped up the rubber mounts from cutting them off<BR>are there replcements?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||05-30-2001||12:56 PM||||Get the poly set from the Fiero Store. Makes a huge difference. No cradle flex.||||reg||1
Z||000005||84Bill||05-30-2001||01:13 PM||||One thing worth noting is that you can spray wd40 on the nutplates thru the frame rail. You can access them on the outside rail thru the crush cutouts. I've done 3 cradle drops so far and havent had any get bound up to where I had to cut them out.<BR>Just stick the straw up in there and spray like a mad man.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Note the cans of wd40  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/Pictures/image020.jpg"> ||||reg||14
